# GPT Researcher Local Corpus Configuration Example
# Copy this file to .env and adjust the paths for your setup

# =============================================================================
# CORPUS CONFIGURATION
# =============================================================================

# Main document path (this is where GPT Researcher will look for documents)
# The DocumentLoader will recursively search all subdirectories
DOC_PATH=/usr/src/app/my-docs

# Multiple corpus paths (mount these as volumes in docker-compose.yml)
# These will be mounted as subdirectories under DOC_PATH
CORPUS_PATH_1=/host/corpus1
CORPUS_PATH_2=/host/corpus2  
CORPUS_PATH_3=/host/corpus3

# =============================================================================
# APACHE TIKA CONFIGURATION
# =============================================================================

# Tika server URL for OCR processing of scanned documents
TIKA_SERVER_URL=http://host.docker.internal:9998

# =============================================================================
# RESEARCH MODES
# =============================================================================

# Report source options:
# - "web": Web search only (default)
# - "local": Local documents only
# - "hybrid": Local documents + web search (recommended)

# You can set this in your code or here as default
# REPORT_SOURCE=hybrid

# =============================================================================
# EXAMPLE USAGE
# =============================================================================

# 1. Local-only research:
#    researcher = GPTResearcher(query="...", report_source="local")
#
# 2. Hybrid research:
#    researcher = GPTResearcher(query="...", report_source="hybrid")
#
# 3. Web-only research (default):
#    researcher = GPTResearcher(query="...", report_source="web")

# =============================================================================
# DOCKER COMPOSE VOLUME MOUNTING EXAMPLE
# =============================================================================

# In your docker-compose.yml, mount your corpus directories like this:
#
# volumes:
#   - ${PWD}/my-docs:/usr/src/app/my-docs:rw
#   - ${CORPUS_PATH_1}:/usr/src/app/my-docs/corpus1:ro
#   - ${CORPUS_PATH_2}:/usr/src/app/my-docs/corpus2:ro
#   - ${CORPUS_PATH_3}:/usr/src/app/my-docs/corpus3:ro
#
# This creates a structure like:
# /usr/src/app/my-docs/
# ├── corpus1/          # Your first corpus
# ├── corpus2/          # Your second corpus  
# ├── corpus3/          # Your third corpus
# └── other-docs/       # Any other documents you put in my-docs

# =============================================================================
# SUPPORTED FILE FORMATS
# =============================================================================

# GPT Researcher can process these file types:
# - PDF (including scanned PDFs via Tika OCR)
# - Word documents (.doc, .docx)
# - PowerPoint (.pptx)
# - Excel (.xls, .xlsx)
# - CSV files
# - Markdown (.md)
# - Plain text (.txt)
# - HTML (.html, .htm)

# =============================================================================
# TESTING YOUR SETUP
# =============================================================================

# Run the test script to verify everything works:
# python test_local_corpus.py

